From 28ffd7b77b8c8acd669ed9728a614b77f9666298 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Miles <scott.miles@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:48:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Bass/Middle/Treble tone stack after the model

Ported from the NAM desktop plugin (NeuralAmpModeler/ToneStack.cpp, MIT):
low shelf at 150 Hz (+/-20 dB), peaking at 425 Hz (+/-15 dB) and high shelf
at 1800 Hz (+/-10 dB). Knobs go 0 to 10, and 5 (the default) is flat, so
existing pedalboards sound the same. The new ports are appended (7, 8, 9),
so the indices of the existing ports do not change. The MOD face shows the
three knobs between Input and Output.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
